e 3 shows the characteristics of the benchmark programs. The size column indicates\n1022:the sizes of the benchmark programs measured in numbers of lines of C code. The description\n1039:                                     Table 3: Benchmarks.\n1041:  column briefly describes the benchmark programs.\n1042:      For each benchmark program, we have selected a number of input data for profiling. Table\n1044:  inputs that are used for each benchmark program. The description column briefly describes\n1045:  the input data. For each benchmark program, we have selected one additional input and used\n1046:  that input to measure the performance. The execution time of the benchmark programs that\n1047:' are annotated with probes for collecting profile information is from 25 to 35 times slower than\n1048:  that of the original benchmark programs. It should be noted that our profiler implementation\n1050:    Table 5 shows the output code quality of our prototype compiler. We compare the output\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
